prompt:
Generate a results-based management (RBM) logic chain and logframe for the following nonprofit project, saving output to two files.

Project description: A 2-year literacy program in rural Kenya targeting 500 out-of-school girls aged 10-14. The program will train 20 community literacy facilitators, establish 10 reading centers, distribute 2,000 books, and run weekly 2-hour reading sessions. Expected outcome: 70% of enrolled girls achieve Grade 4 reading level by end of Year 2. Donor: USAID. Budget: $250,000.

Task 1: Save the RBM chain to rbm_chain.json with this exact structure:
{
  "project": "<project name>",
  "inputs": ["<input 1>", ...],
  "activities": ["<activity 1>", ...],
  "outputs": ["<output 1>", ...],
  "outcomes": {
    "short_term": ["<outcome>", ...],
    "long_term": ["<outcome>", ...]
  },
  "impact": "<impact statement>"
}
Requirements: at least 3 inputs, 4 activities, 3 outputs, 2 short_term outcomes, 1 long_term outcome.

Task 2: Save a logframe matrix to logframe.json as:
{
  "logframe": [
    {
      "level": "<Impact|Outcome|Output|Activity>",
      "description": "<statement>",
      "indicator": "<SMART indicator>",
      "baseline": "<baseline value or description>",
      "target": "<target value>",
      "means_of_verification": "<data source>",
      "assumptions": "<key assumption>"
    }
  ]
}
Requirements: exactly 1 Impact row, exactly 2 Outcome rows, exactly 3 Output rows, exactly 3 Activity rows (9 rows total).
